  "schema_limitations": [
    "edge has no evidence, provenance, confidence, or attributes columns; subsystem edge evidence therefore remains in triage by function VA, package provenance is stored on Package nodes, and association evidence is encoded in the two relation names.",
    "The xref table, rather than generic edge rows, is the lossless representation of function dependencies because it preserves caller, callee, callsite, reference type, source, and snapshot hash.",
    "field can represent an offset, role, type value, and separate offset/meaning evidence, but cannot represent a first-class field node or arbitrary bit ranges; no such extension was introduced.",
    "node uniqueness is only (label, name), with no native namespace or alias table; missing canonical functions were added under the existing fun:VA convention and the unresolved Cell addresses were not aliased.",
    "The schema has no first-class relationship-evidence table, so unresolved, inferred, runtime, and package-scope candidate relations cannot be safely mixed with the imported evidence-backed edge types."
  ],
